Subject: Wifi: MP host may count a client as answered without a frame

ndsrecomp modification to vendored melonDS src/Wifi.cpp and src/Wifi.h
(GPLv3 5(a) notice; see patches/README.md for the convention).

After MP_RecvReplies the host asks the runner-owned hook
nds_wifi_local_mp_take_ack_only() for clients that answered the cmd but
whose reply frame has not arrived yet. Those clients are cleared from
MPClientFail (so the ACK and the cmd slot status report success and
neither side retransmits) and kept in MPClientNoFrame, which skips
MPClientReplyRX for them (so no stale MPClientReplies slot is handed to
the guest as a duplicate). The runner only returns a non-zero mask in
--local-wireless-late-replies mode, where it queues each client's replies
FIFO and delivers them one per later cmd; otherwise behaviour is
unchanged.

--- a/src/Wifi.h
+++ b/src/Wifi.h
@@ class Wifi, MP host state
     u16 MPClientMask, MPClientFail;
+    u16 MPClientNoFrame; // answered without a frame (patch 0027)
--- a/src/Wifi.cpp
+++ b/src/Wifi.cpp
@@ (runner hook declarations)
+uint16_t nds_wifi_local_mp_take_ack_only();
@@ Wifi::Reset
     MPClientFail = 0;
+    MPClientNoFrame = 0;
@@ Wifi::ProcessTX, MP reply window
-                if (!(MPClientFail & curclient))
+                if (!(MPClientFail & curclient) && !(MPClientNoFrame & curclient))
                     MPClientReplyRX(nclient);
@@ Wifi::ProcessTX, MP cmd transmit done
                 u16 res = 0;
+                MPClientNoFrame = 0;
                 if (MPClientMask)
+                {
                     res = Platform::MP_RecvReplies(MPClientReplies, USTimestamp, MPClientMask, NDS.UserData);
-                MPClientFail &= ~res;
+                    MPClientNoFrame = ::nds_wifi_local_mp_take_ack_only() & MPClientMask & ~res;
+                }
+                MPClientFail &= ~(res | MPClientNoFrame);
